WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.765
Detections are only as effective as the telemetry supporting them.

00:00:03.765 --> 00:00:08.162
Security teams may use endpoint logs, authentication records, network events, cloud telemetry,

00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:11.461
application logs, email security events, and identity provider data.

00:00:11.461 --> 00:00:15.858
Detection engineers need to understand what data exists, how it is collected,

00:00:15.858 --> 00:00:19.156
how quickly it arrives, and what fields are available.

00:00:19.156 --> 00:00:23.554
A detection that depends on data the organization does not collect will

00:00:23.554 --> 00:00:26.852
fail no matter how carefully the logic is written.

00:00:26.852 --> 00:00:28.318
Telemetry also has limitations.

00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:30.884
Logs may be incomplete, delayed, normalized differently,

00:00:30.884 --> 00:00:34.548
retained for different lengths of time, or missing important context.

00:00:34.548 --> 00:00:37.480
These constraints affect confidence and should be documented.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.244
Good visibility planning helps teams choose detections that are realistic for their environment.

00:00:42.244 --> 00:00:47.008
It also exposes gaps that may require new logging, improved enrichment, better parsing,

00:00:47.008 --> 00:00:49.940
or closer collaboration with infrastructure and application owners.
